import{_ as i,o as a,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 466 | Dragon Ball · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Dragon-Ball Wishing and Causal Disruption","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 466 | Dragon Ball · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Dragon-Ball Wishing and Causal Disruption","no":466,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Causal Self-Discipline","Dragon-Ball Wish","Causal Disruption","Revival Mechanism"],"related":["19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0466_模块2-龙珠-因果自律缺失-龙珠许愿与因果扰乱.md","filePath":"en/0466_模块2-龙珠-因果自律缺失-龙珠许愿与因果扰乱.md"}'),s={name:"en/0466_模块2-龙珠-因果自律缺失-龙珠许愿与因果扰乱.md"};function o(r,e,l,u,d,h){return a(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-466-dragon-ball-·-causal-self-discipline-absence-dragon-ball-wishing-and-causal-disruption" tabindex="-1">Entry 466 | Dragon Ball · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Dragon-Ball Wishing and Causal Disruption <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-466-dragon-ball-·-causal-self-discipline-absence-dragon-ball-wishing-and-causal-disruption" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 466 | Dragon Ball · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Dragon-Ball Wishing and Causal Disruption&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 35 · Civilization Analysis 8) | Benchmark base: Documents 19, 03, 49</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-revival-needs-no-price" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when revival needs no price <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-revival-needs-no-price" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when revival needs no price&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The causal self-discipline axiom requires: cross-plane operations strictly filed, observe first then limited interference, only return knowledge without disturbing causality. Dragon Ball world is precisely this axiom&#39;s complete opposite — Dragon-Ball wishing turns &quot;revival,&quot; &quot;restoration,&quot; &quot;reality rewriting&quot; into zero-threshold operations. The dead can revive, cities can restore, time can reverse; Frieza can revive, Cell can revive, Buu can revive. This entry takes the <strong>causal self-discipline axiom</strong> as core, deeply analyzing Dragon Ball world&#39;s causal disruption.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Causal disruption&#39;s energy waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Revival = history zeroed</strong>: every wish to revive the dead erases civilization&#39;s trauma memory; history does not advance</li><li><strong>Causal chain broken</strong>: after the dead revive, their original causality (funeral, mourning, inheritance) all erased</li><li><strong>Wish = shortcut</strong>: whoever gathers Dragon Balls takes the biggest cosmos-tier resource — this resource does not rely on cultivation, contribution, legislation</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How causal disruption feeds historical regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Law of causality hollowed out</strong>: because the dead can revive, &quot;death&quot; is no longer the end; civilization&#39;s reverence for life diluted</li><li><strong>Effort loses meaning</strong>: since can wish revival, why cherish life? Since can wish restore, why build cities?</li><li><strong>History discontinuous</strong>: because setting changes anytime, revival rules added with plot; civilization has no true &quot;history&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s role in causal disruption:</p><ul><li><strong>Accepting wishing no threshold</strong>: Goku&#39;s party repeatedly gathers Dragon Balls to &quot;revive companions&quot;; never reflects &quot;how much causality this revival disrupted&quot;</li><li><strong>Revival = solving problems</strong>: after fighting Buu, after fighting Zamasu, after fighting Jiren, it always ends &quot;wish restore everything&quot; — Goku never truly solves problems; just erases problems by wish</li><li><strong>No reverence for causality</strong>: Goku never treats the dragon god as &quot;a causal being to revere,&quot; but as &quot;a tool person to use when he wants&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Causal Disruption</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Causal Self-Discipline Plan</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gather then wish</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom: cross-plane operations strictly filed; observe first then limited interference</td></tr><tr><td>Revival no threshold</td><td>Revival goes Symbiotic Court approval: who revives, why, what price</td></tr><tr><td>Wish = power</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republicanism: any reality-rewriting operation goes Anchor Council legislation</td></tr><tr><td>History erased</td><td>Civilization trauma memory retained; revival does not rewrite history</td></tr><tr><td>Dragon god as tool person</td><td>Dragon-god-tier power under Alaya supervision; not diverted by any private party</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball wishing history — revive companions, revive Frieza, restore Earth, restore universe</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;if wishing needs causal self-discipline approval; revival goes Symbiotic Court&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count Dragon Balls privately diverted times, civilization trauma memory retention rate, law-of-causality modified times</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Dragon Ball Causal Disruption Report</em>, quantifying &quot;every wish devalues Dragon Ball world&#39;s law of causality&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Causal setting self-consistency: low</strong> (revival rules change with plot: one wish a year → three wishes → cross-universe wishes → Black-Star Dragon Balls planet explodes after wish)</li><li><strong>Causal self-consistency expected: high</strong> (revival goes approval, trauma memory retained, Alaya trail-marked)</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong> (revival rules repeatedly changed between original, GT, Super)</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high</strong> — Dragon Ball wishing mainly used by Goku&#39;s party; Myriad Ranks no access</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: revival zeroes history, invalidates effort, erases trauma memory</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: public miracle (dragon god) privately diverted as wishing tool</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least raised cultivation by effort; Goku solves problems by wishing</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: among Myriad Ranks only those who gather Dragon Balls can use the dragon god</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: world with collapsed law of causality cannot truly expand into stable multiverse</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Dragon Ball wishing mechanism is Dragon Ball worldview&#39;s most charming and most dangerous design — it realized childhood wishes, also hollowed out civilization&#39;s law of causality. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is the causal self-discipline axiom: any reality-rewriting operation must be filed, approved, trail-marked; revival is not forbidden, but must go legal process, must retain trauma memory, must let Myriad-Ranks parliament know. Let the dragon god return to &quot;Myriad Ranks&#39; public miracle&quot; position; this is Dragon Ball causal disruption&#39;s true way out.</p><p>One more layer: Dragon Ball wishing mechanism&#39;s deepest harm is not &quot;reviving people&quot; itself, but that it makes &quot;death&quot; lose weight. When readers know &quot;anyway can revive,&quot; when characters know &quot;anyway can revive,&quot; when writers know &quot;anyway can revive&quot; — death is no longer narrative&#39;s ultimate seriousness, but only &quot;temporary exit.&quot; Gohan dies in Cell Game? Revive. Buu kills all Earthlings? Revive. Frieza kills Namekians? Revive. Over forty years, Dragon Ball world&#39;s death scenes can no longer truly make readers tense — because everyone knows, the last Dragon Ball will solve everything. This is causal-self-discipline absence&#39;s corrosion on narrative seriousness, and also on civilizational reverence.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · causal self-discipline absence · Dragon-Ball wishing and causal disruption described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./444_模块2-龙珠-龙珠设定批判-随意许愿的因果扰乱.html">Entry 444 · Dragon-Ball Setting Critique</a> · <a href="./465_模块2-龙珠-文明权重分析-悟空个人权重碾压文明共识.html">Entry 465 · Civilizational Weight</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/19-修炼伦理与边界.html">19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const v=i(s,[["render",o]]);export{g as __pageData,v as default};
